.TH CTBREC-AUTO-PORTRAITS 1 "2026-11-09" "ctbrec-auto-portraits" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctbrec-auto-portraits \- backfill missing model portraits on a ctbrec server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctbrec-auto-portraits
[\fIOPTIONS\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctbrec-auto-portraits
runs on the ctbrec server host (normally inside the Proxmox container) and
gives every recorded model a portrait. It reads the recording metadata under
the ctbrec config directory, collects the newest recording for each model URL,
and skips models that already have a portrait.
.P
For each missing model it issues one authenticated
.B GET
request to the ctbrec server's
.B /image/portrait/fetch/
endpoint. The server downloads the model's site preview thumbnail, crops and
scales it to a 256x256 JPEG, writes it to the portrait store and records the
mapping in
.IR models.json .
The script itself never writes the config; the running server owns that file.
.P
Some sites, notably Stripchat, serve previews as webp. Java's image library has
no webp decoder, so the server passes those bytes through untouched and stores
them in a file named
.IR .jpg ,
which the desktop client cannot read. When the downloaded bytes are webp the
script converts them with
.BR ffmpeg (1)
to a real 256x256 centre-cropped JPEG and uploads that over the same portrait
id. The
.B \-\-normalize
mode repairs portraits that were fetched before this conversion existed.
.P
Only models that appear in recording metadata are considered. A failure is
remembered in a small state file and that model is skipped for
.B \-\-retry\-after
hours, so frequent runs do not hammer a site that is rate limiting the server.
.P
The script talks to the server over HTTPS with certificate verification
disabled by default, because a stock ctbrec installation uses a self-signed
certificate. It requires Python 3 and no third-party modules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-dir " PATH"
ctbrec version config directory containing
.I models.json
and
.IR server.json .
By default the newest non-backup directory under
.I ~/.config/ctbrec
that contains both files is used.
.TP
.BI \-\-server " URL"
Base URL of the running ctbrec server. Default:
.IR https://127.0.0.1:8443 .
.TP
.BI \-\-delay " SECONDS"
Pause between models. Default:
.IR 1.5 .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Per-model HTTP timeout. Default:
.IR 90 .
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Process at most
.I N
models this run. Default:
.B 0
(no limit). The bundled systemd timer uses 100.
.TP
.BI \-\-retry\-after " HOURS"
Do not retry a failed model for this many hours. Default:
.IR 6 .
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-file " PATH"
Failure backoff state file. Default:
.IR ~/.local/state/ctbrec-auto-portraits.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-ffmpeg " PATH"
ffmpeg executable used to convert webp previews. Default:
.IR ffmpeg
from
.IR PATH .
If it is not found, webp portraits are stored unconverted (with a warning).
.TP
.B \-\-normalize
Convert every existing webp file in the portraits directory to a 256x256 JPEG
in place, then exit. Makes no network requests and does not touch
.IR models.json .
.TP
.B \-\-force
Ignore existing portraits and the failure backoff and re-fetch every recorded
model.
.TP
.B \-\-verify\-tls
Verify the server certificate instead of accepting a self-signed one.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print which models would be fetched and change nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Print only the final summary line.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS Model selection
.IP \(bu 2
Recorded means: at least one JSON file in
.IR <config-dir>/recordings/ ,
which contains the model URL. The newest recording per URL is kept only to
order the work; the portrait itself comes from the site, not the file.
.IP \(bu 2
Models whose portrait mapping exists and whose portrait file is present are
skipped even if the mapping points at a stale id without a file: the missing
file makes them eligible again.
.IP \(bu 2
Work is ordered newest recording first, so models recorded today get a
portrait before long-dormant ones.
.SS Concurrency
A lock file next to the state file prevents two runs from overlapping. A
second invocation exits immediately with status 0.
.SS Image format
.IP \(bu 2
JPEG previews are stored by the server exactly as returned, already cropped to
256x256.
.IP \(bu 2
webp previews are converted locally and re-uploaded, so the stored file is a
real JPEG that both the web interface and the desktop client can decode.
.IP \(bu 2
If ffmpeg is unavailable the webp bytes are kept; run
.B \-\-normalize
after installing ffmpeg to repair them.
.SS Authentication
If
.I server.json
contains a non-empty
.B key
(ctbrec HMAC authentication), every request is signed with
.B CTBREC-HMAC
using HMAC-SHA256 in hex, matching the web interface.
.SH EXAMPLES
See what would be fetched:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-auto-portraits \-\-dry\-run \-\-limit 10
.EE
.P
Fetch portraits for up to 25 models:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-auto-portraits \-\-limit 25
.EE
.P
Re-fetch everything, including models that already have a portrait:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-auto-portraits \-\-force
.EE
.P
Repair webp portraits fetched by an older version of the script:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-auto-portraits \-\-normalize
.EE
.P
Run from the desktop through the SSH wrapper:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-auto-portraits-remote \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including runs where individual models failed (those are recorded in
the state file and retried later).
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error: no config directory, unreadable
.IR models.json ,
or a missing remote executable.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ctbrec/<version>/models.json
Model list and portrait id map. Read only.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ctbrec/<version>/recordings/*.json
Recording metadata used to enumerate recorded models.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ctbrec/portraits/<uuid>.jpg
Portrait files written by the server.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ctbrec-auto-portraits.json
Failure backoff state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctbrec-auto-portraits-remote (1),
.BR ctbrec-webui-patch (1),
.BR ctbrec-merge (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
